MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Jim Croce feels like a natural next choice because his melodic storytelling connects with what I enjoy about Simon & Garfunkel and Jonathan Edwards.",
    "Jethro Tull's retrospective fits my interest in older rock collections, while Johnny Cash appeals to the reflective, song-centered side of my listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Titles such as Rewind and Greatest Hits, Vol. 1 and 2 leave me unsure whose music I would be choosing; a collection alone is not enough to establish a personal connection.",
    "Blues Deluxe suggests a blues-focused direction that interests me less right now than familiar folk and classic rock, and 25 does not connect as strongly with my current wish to revisit older songs."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My repeated interest in greatest-hits albums seems to have been taken as enthusiasm for almost any collection, when the artist and songs are what make me choose one.",
    "My interest in older rock seems to have been stretched toward music that feels broadly related without the melodic storytelling or familiarity I am seeking."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection between Simon & Garfunkel, Jonathan Edwards, and Melanie matters to me: recognizable voices, memorable melodies, and songs with a personal story.",
    "Although I have also listened to pop, right now I am more drawn to revisiting familiar older songs; that preference matters more than my willingness to try different music in the past."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The choices partly capture my interest in older music and retrospectives, but sometimes mistake a collection format or broad musical connection for the familiar songs and storytelling I want."
}
